        "composition": "A lightweight LSH structure supplies good starting points for both incremental graph insertion and later searches, reducing traversal distance. Projected-distance screening further reduces expensive full-dimensional checks. The graph then refines the approximate seeds. Benefits cost extra index space and potential false dismissals; the paper’s cardinality-insensitive cost model is not a worst-case constant-time guarantee for arbitrary data.",
