        "composition": "Flexible meeting points can reduce vehicle detours and permit more shared rides, but considering every nearby pickup/drop-off pair multiplies insertion work. SMDB first selects a bounded candidate set heuristically and constructs an HMPO road hierarchy with convenient core vertices. Set-maximum-difference bounds then allow online insertion to rule out multiple candidates together when even their best bounded improvement cannot meet the deadline. This pruning preserves feasibility within the selected search space; it does not make the offline candidate heuristic or irrevocable online route assignment globally optimal. Passenger walking remains part of the objective and service contract.",
