        "composition": "FastFlow first identifies CPU preprocessing as the limiting stage. If the potential gain is worthwhile, measured costs select among three pipeline placements and determine a local/remote data ratio. Counter-based dispatch enforces that ratio during training. The policy is selected before the run for allocated resources; runtime autoscaling and adaptive worker rebalancing are discussed as future extensions. It preserves the preprocessing and learning logic while spending remote CPU capacity and network bandwidth. Cached profiles reduce setup work but depend on representative measurements and matching job/resource configurations.",
