        "composition": "Exact stable coloring often leaves almost as many colors as vertices. Quasi-stability relaxes identical neighborhood totals to a specified similarity relation, and Rothko repeatedly splits a color involved in a large discrepancy until it reaches a target color count or structural-error threshold. Reduced instances can then be solved more cheaply. The structural tolerance is not a universal answer-error certificate: the LP convergence theorem needs a well-behaved problem and sufficiently small relative tolerance; max-flow can be arbitrarily overestimated without extra assumptions; even exact 1-WL colors need not share centrality. Rothko is a heuristic, so it neither guarantees the coarsest admissible coloring nor monotonic improvement of every downstream objective.",
