        "composition": "SetPush first rewrites single-node PageRank using undirected-graph reversibility. It truncates the infinite walk-length sum, then fully pushes sufficiently large per-edge residue and samples smaller contributions with appropriate reweighting. Geometric skipping avoids enumerating unselected neighbors. The random estimator is unbiased for the truncated sum, while truncation itself introduces bounded bias relative to full PageRank. The combined guarantee is probabilistic relative accuracy. The expected query bound depends on undirected, locally accessible adjacency data and fixed accuracy/teleport parameters; it is not a deterministic worst-case bound or a result for arbitrary directed PageRank.",
