        "composition": "VersaMatch normalizes ontology elements into reusable enriched profiles, blocks unlikely pairs with MinHash LSH, and combines weak supervision with a learned matcher. Soft functions feed a probabilistic label model; sparse hard functions override it through majority voting. Confident generated labels train a discriminative model, while a coverage-weighted ensemble retains weak rules for rare cases. This reduces dependence on gold training labels but still requires trustworthy labeling functions and usable ontology descriptions. Blocking is approximate, hard-rule precision is an assumption, and no coherence-repair stage guarantees logically consistent mappings. Additional learning and profile construction can make it slower than traditional ontology matchers.",
