        "composition": "OpBoost exploits the fact that tree splits depend on feature order. Feature owners normalize and randomize ordered values, send their ranks, and later provide noisy split-point values so the label holder can construct the boosted trees. Global-map uses distance-aware noise; Adj-map separately controls noise within and between semantic partitions. Local-map keeps values inside their original partition and therefore reveals partition membership. These are different privacy contracts from uniform LDP, not an accuracy improvement at an identical guarantee. Ordering is probabilistic, preprocessing can lose information, and multiple features require composed privacy accounting. Discrete Laplace sampling avoids domain-sized sampling work, but bounded sampling can need repeated draws at strong privacy settings.",
