        "composition": "DICN encodes aligned aerial images and GPS trajectory maps in two streams, then learns cross-source attention instead of simply concatenating the features. Edge supervision comes from morphological processing of road-mask labels; contrastive training emphasizes confusing foreground/background pixels near boundaries. Mixed-source pretraining supplies weights reused for the main segmentation task. These losses encourage smoothness and class separation but do not enforce a topological invariant or guarantee connected, correct road networks. The output is a binary pixel mask, not a validated routable graph. Labeled masks, aligned inputs, noisy or sparse trajectories, model capacity, and training cost affect results; optional test-time augmentation adds inference work.",
