        "composition": "HEDA encodes data and predicate constants at the client, evaluates encrypted comparisons in a suitable binary or numerical domain, and lifts their encrypted masks into the larger aggregation domain without decrypting them. Mask multiplication implements filtering; coefficient/slot conversion enables multi-attribute arithmetic. Bootstrapping relaxes fixed-depth limitations, but “unbounded” does not mean unlimited precision, arbitrary SQL support, or low latency. The semi-honest-server contract protects entries and predicate values under FHE assumptions while revealing database size, schema/types, and predicate count. Evaluated queries need about seven minutes for 8,192 rows, dominated by per-row bootstrapping. Scaled-number ranges and cryptographic parameters must be chosen appropriately; efficient general GROUP BY, ORDER BY, and multi-way joins remain open in this work.",
