        "composition": "TOD factors supported detectors into shared tensor building blocks and executes them on GPUs. It reduces memory in two distinct ways: dependency-aware batching/fusion avoids large intermediates, and provable quantization certifies low-precision discrete decisions before accepting them. Ambiguous cases fall back to original precision. This preserves supported operator outputs rather than intentionally relaxing detector accuracy, but it does not guarantee that the detector’s outlier labels match ground truth. Quantization is unsuitable when verifying an output such as a full-precision distance would require the original computation anyway. The paper does not support tree-based detectors or gradient-descent operators, and its multi-GPU evaluation assumes homogeneous devices.",
