        "composition": "ND-tree represents a subtree by the set of symbols appearing in each dimension, avoiding an arbitrary numeric ordering of categorical values. Hamming-distance lower bounds reject rectangles that cannot contain a match; exact vector checks finish the search. Insertion and split heuristics prioritize low overlap and use discrete alphabet structure to limit candidate partitions. These are structural heuristics, not a calibrated query-cost optimizer, and they do not guarantee globally optimal splits. The evaluated genome task searches fixed-length vectors by Hamming distance, not arbitrary sequence alignment or edit distance. Broad-radius queries can favor scanning, the index consumes substantial space, and reported gains are I/O comparisons rather than measured end-to-end speedups.",
