        "principleNotes": {
            "Ha": "Map relational attributes to the two-dimensional MEMS tip/sector geometry while respecting the limit on concurrently active tips and directional movement costs.",
            "Wv": "Retrieve only referenced attributes rather than transferring complete disk-style pages that include unused columns.",
            "Lo": "Place aligned record fields and consecutive rows to exploit coordinated tip access and favorable sled traversal, packing retrieved fields for useful cache access."
        },
        "composition": "FRM exposes the fine-grained two-dimensional placement available in the modeled MEMS device. It stripes each attribute over aligned tip sectors and selects active tips according to the query’s columns, using additional passes when the active-tip limit is exceeded. This avoids importing irrelevant fields into memory and cache while retaining complete values for query evaluation. The physical-device results are analytical estimates for the CMU CHIPS model, not measurements on a deployed MEMS product. Cache behavior is separately measured using memory-resident layouts on a CPU. Benefits shrink as more attributes are requested, and PAX can have better cache behavior at low selectivity/projectivity. The design requires device-specific control, layout metadata, and sector/row alignment.",
